    sha256: 0474580014a697c47370992feee115d49c80b105b9c43270bf89afff0e4b0aa5
  body: "# Continuing employment before the hours question\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured
    JSA/IS guidance asks whether work is continuing before assessing remunerative-work hours and treats
    continuing employment as a factual question informed by the actual relationship and work pattern.\n\
    \n## Scope and exceptions\n\nA gap between jobs, a contract label or a P45 is not a substitute for
    the source’s factual enquiry. JSA(Cont) concerns the claimant’s work, while JSA(IB) and IS also address
    a partner’s work. Memo-qualified text and the full exceptions remain dependencies; no employment-status
    or entitlement decision is made.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 20200, PDF page 46](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/67ffaf91694d57c6b1cf8e0e/dmgch20.pdf#page=46)
    — DMG Vol 4: Ch 20, JSA and IS, conditions of entitlement.\n- [DMG 20201, PDF page 46](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/67ffaf91694d57c6b1cf8e0e/dmgch20.pdf#page=46)
    — DMG Vol 4: Ch 20, JSA and IS, conditions of entitlement.\n- [DMG 20202, PDF page 46](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/67ffaf91694d57c6b1cf8e0e/dmgch20.pdf#page=46)
    — DMG Vol 4: Ch 20, JSA and IS, conditions of entitlement.\n- [DMG 20206, PDF page 47](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/67ffaf91694d57c6b1cf8e0e/dmgch20.pdf#page=47)
    — DMG Vol 4: Ch 20, JSA and IS, conditions of entitlement.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted
    interpretation of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review
    is required. Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring
    time are separate.\n\nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document,
    individual advice, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter
    reading order, footnotes and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural
    evaluation pass is claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol4-ch20`: PDF SHA-256 `0474580014a697c47370992feee115d49c80b105b9c43270bf89afff0e4b0aa5`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `ed007251fa43ff9c63f5116f603798f2279c84006af8539bbbfd50194ab0ab56`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/legacy-jsa-remunerative-work
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The chapter requires the continuing-work question to be considered before counting
      hours for remunerative work.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch20/0046
      quote: "20200 [See Memo DMG 13/20] Being in remunerative work affects entitlement to JSA and IS
        1. In all\ncases, before the DM applies the law to establish how many hours a person is working,
        they must decide\nwhether or not the work is continuing.\n\n\n                               \
        \                               1 JS Act 95, s 1(2)(e); SS CB Act 92, s 124(1)(c)\n\n\n\nJSA(Cont)"
      locator: DMG 20200
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch20/0047
      quote: "20206 It is a question of fact for the DM whether the work is continuing or not. DMs will
        need to consider\nsuch things as\n\n\n• the type and nature of the work\n\n\n• the frequency and
        length of the contracts/periods of work\n\n\n• the process of securing the work\n\n\n• the employment
        situation/opportunities in the area\n\n\n• whether there is a continuing relationship between
        the claimant and the employer\n\n\n• whether there is evidence of the relationship between the
        claimant and the employer having ended, e.g.\nthe production of a P45.\n\n\nThis list is not prescriptive
        or exhaustive and other considerations may be equally valid in the\ncircumstances of each case."
      locator: DMG 20206
